course: dictionary
lesson: 3601
title: Fifteen in everyday life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fifteen is the number 15. It is ten and five more, and it is one more than fourteen. You can write it as 15 in figures.
explain: You meet fifteen in maths every day. Three times five makes fifteen, and so does five times three. «You've been arguing with a thesaurus for fifteen minutes.» Here fifteen is used to measure time.
explain: On a clock, quarter past is fifteen minutes past the hour, and fifteen minutes is a quarter of an hour. Fifteen can also name a team: a rugby union team has fifteen players, so a team of fifteen is called a fifteen.
fact: Fifteen is written as 15 in figures.
fact: Fifteen is ten plus five, and one more than fourteen.
fact: 3 × 5 = 15 and 5 × 3 = 15.
fact: «Fifteen minutes» is the same as a quarter of an hour.
fact: A rugby union team, called a fifteen, has fifteen players.
exercise: What number is one more than fourteen? | 13 | 16 | *15 | 17
exercise: Which sum makes 15 when multiplied? | 6 × 6 | 2 × 7 | 4 × 4 | *5 × 3
exercise: «A hot drink can still scald a small child badly fifteen minutes after it was made.» How long after it was made can it still scald? | *Fifteen minutes | Fifty minutes | An hour and a half | Five minutes
test: How many minutes is a quarter of an hour? | 30 | *15 | 5 | 10
test: A rugby union team, called a fifteen, has how many players? | 20 | 11 | 12 | *15
exam: Ten plus five makes which number? | 14 | 50 | *15 | 16
